> Inspect the actual bounded-run diagnostics

These figures read captured original episode returns and logged evaluation/loss values. A single evaluation point is shown as a point; it does not imply a learning trend. Source quality checks deferred in bounded mode remain explicitly labelled in the output.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/noisy_networks_return.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/noisy_networks_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int series=0;for(const auto& [key,tensor]:archive){if(!key.starts_with("return_"))continue;auto values=tensor.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x;for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)x.push_back(i+1);plot.lines(x,values,key,{37+series*50,99,235-series*50}).points(x,values,key+" points",{37+series*50,99,235-series*50},4);++series;}plot.title("noisy networks actual return diagnostics").x_label("Ended training episode").y_label("CartPole task return").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/noisy_networks_return.svg");}
```
